1
00:00:05,100 --> 00:00:07,290
Black pod is a rain-driven disease.

2
00:00:07,340 --> 00:00:12,760
Every year it destroys an estimated twenty to thirty percent of the world's cocoa.

3
00:00:14,020 --> 00:00:15,310
Here is the problem.

4
00:00:15,360 --> 00:00:21,990
After heavy rain, a Malaysian smallholder has about thirty minutes to scout, but cannot check every block.

5
00:00:22,040 --> 00:00:29,050
He walks his usual round, so infected pods in the wettest blocks are found late, and the disease spreads.

6
00:00:33,300 --> 00:00:35,150
KokoShield solves this.

7
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:40,120
When rain passes thirty millimetres in twenty-four hours, it activates.

8
00:00:41,200 --> 00:00:43,540
A borrowed drone marks standing water.

9
00:00:43,590 --> 00:00:53,430
KokoShield combines it with the rain gauge, each block's drainage and past confirmed cases, and builds a thirty-minute route that visits the riskiest blocks first.

10
00:00:53,480 --> 00:00:55,640
Block A, then D.

11
00:00:56,930 --> 00:01:04,840
Our own Field Node, a 3D-printed sensor concept, adds local temperature and humidity at block level.

12
00:01:08,050 --> 00:01:10,510
Same farm, same thirty minutes.

13
00:01:10,560 --> 00:01:14,970
The usual round finds its first suspect pod at minute four, and two in total.

14
00:01:15,020 --> 00:01:19,080
The ranked route finds one at minute two, and seven in total.

15
00:01:22,140 --> 00:01:27,310
In block A, the scout logs three suspect pods on his phone, even offline.

16
00:01:27,360 --> 00:01:31,780
The adviser confirms, and only the affected blocks are treated.

17
00:01:33,640 --> 00:01:40,170
Earlier detection means fewer pods lost, higher smallholder income, and more resilient food systems.

18
00:01:40,220 --> 00:01:44,240
The same planner already supports rice blast in China.

19
00:01:45,510 --> 00:01:49,990
We're asking for twelve hundred ringgit to complete the first single-farm pilot.

20
00:01:50,040 --> 00:01:51,240
KokoShield.

21
00:01:51,290 --> 00:01:53,510
Find disease sooner after the rain.
